<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Deliberately NOT sandboxed.

	  App-scoped security bookmarks (com.apple.security.files.bookmarks.app-scope)
	  bind to the app's code-signing identity. This target signs ad-hoc
	  (CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = "-", no DEVELOPMENT_TEAM), so there is no stable identity
	  to bind to and URL.bookmarkData(options: .withSecurityScope) fails with
	  NSCocoaErrorDomain 256 "Could not open() the item" — even though the file is
	  readable and the security scope opens successfully.

	  Under the sandbox a plain bookmark cannot restore access across launches, so
	  enabling the sandbox without a Developer Team ID means imported sounds break on
	  every relaunch. Running unsandboxed with plain bookmarks works correctly.

	  If a Developer Team ID is ever configured, re-add:
	      com.apple.security.app-sandbox
	      com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-only
	      com.apple.security.files.bookmarks.app-scope
	  SoundDeckModel already prefers security-scoped bookmarks when they work and
	  falls back to plain ones, so it will pick the scoped path up automatically.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
